# The image is built from the Go source and the assets embedded in it, and
# from nothing else. Checked against the Dockerfile, which copies go.mod and
# go.sum and then the tree, and against every go:embed in the repository:
# api/openapi.yaml, internal/fontset/partition.json, internal/httpapi/page.html,
# internal/ocr/models/, internal/render/fonts/. All of those live under source
# directories, so none of what follows is needed to build.

# History. 116 MB, and the commit is passed to the build as an argument
# instead (see internal/buildid).
.git
.github

# Built and generated output, and the measurement scripts.
out/

# Test data. The synthetic corpus and the real labels are hundreds of
# megabytes of PNG, and the binary reads neither.
synth/
real/
real2/
eval/
testdata/

# The retired training environments. 1.4 GB on disk, none of it tracked, and
# nothing the binary carries comes from here since step 19a deleted the
# models these built.
python/

# The ONNX Runtime library. The Dockerfile fetches the Linux build itself;
# what is here is a developer's copy for another platform.
third_party/

# Prose.
docs/
*.md
